# Bilingual i18n & CJK Bitmap Font Rules / 双语国际化与字库规范

1. **Default Language**: Simplified Chinese (`zh-CN`) is default; English (`en`) is built into C++ source keys and selected dynamically at runtime (`src/core/i18n.cc`).
2. **Strict ASCII Sort Order**: Entries in `src/core/lang_zh_cn.h` (`kZhCnTable`) **must** be strictly sorted in ascending ASCII byte (`strcmp`) order for `O(log N)` binary search. Duplicate keys or out-of-order rows will break lookups and fail CI.
3. **Never Hand-Edit `src/core/cjk_font_data.h`**: It is autogenerated by `tools/gen_cjk_font.py` (which emits both 12×12 and `#if !defined(BRUCE_COMPACT_CJK_FONT)` 16×16 PROGMEM bitmaps).
4. **Mandatory Regeneration & Verification**: After any edit to `src/core/lang_zh_cn.h` or CJK characters in scanned files (`settings.cc`, `ConfigMenu.cc`, `i18n.cc`), run:
   ```sh
   python3 tools/gen_cjk_font.py
   python3 tools/gen_cjk_font.py --check
   python3 tools/gen_cjk_font.py --check-tables
   ```
   (Requires Python 3 + `Pillow` + a system CJK font or `BRUCE_CJK_FONT=/path/to/font.ttc`.)
5. **UTF-8 Safety**: Always measure, wrap, and truncate translated text with `bruce_i18n::utf8PixelWidth`, `utf8TruncateToWidth`, `utf8WrapToWidth`, and `utf8SafeCutBytes` — never slice raw UTF-8 byte offsets mid-codepoint.
